id: pm-y26mvc
title: "pm comments/notes <id> --add --file <path> is refused as positional-and---add conflict instead of naming the swallowed --file flag, so the annotation flag-like check from pm-vcu7 loses precedence"
description: "Found 2026-11-07 while reading telemetry: comments is the top failing command (255 finish failures in 24 h, automation context). Repro on 2026.11.7: pm comments <id> --add --file note.md exits 2 with code command_failed and detail 'Specify comment text either as positional [text] or with --add, not both'. Commander binds --file as the value of --add, so note.md becomes positional text and the positional/--add conflict check fires first. The same shape hits --add --stdin x and pm notes/learnings. Without a trailing operand the pm-vcu7 guard does fire (annotation_flag_like_value), but its recovery says 'Use --stdin to read stdin' even when the swallowed flag was --file, so the agent is not told that --file <path> works on its own. pm-vcu7 is closed and its AC covered notes --add --stdin, learnings --add --file and comments --add --stdin without a trailing operand; this is the operand-following composition it did not test. Duplicate check: searched comments --add --file, flag-like annotation values, positional and --add conflict across all statuses; pm-vcu7 (closed, fixed), pm-hcco and pm-yp56 are the nearest and do not cover this precedence."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,annotations,comments,recovery,recurrence
created_at: "2026-11-07T09:07:11.835Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T19:07:04.326Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-07T19:07:03.694Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-07T19:07:03.694Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "pm comments|notes|learnings <id> --add --file <path> and --add --stdin <operand> refuse with annotation_flag_like_value (not command_failed), before the positional/--add conflict check; The recovery names the swallowed flag's own form: for --file it says to drop --add and pass --file <path>, for --stdin to drop --add; The executable retry, when offered, runs successfully against a sandbox tracker; Regression tests cover each annotation command with a trailing operand, with a negative control that restores the old check order"
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
repro_steps: pm comments <id> --add --file note.md --json
resolution: "assertNoSwallowedAnnotationOption (src/cli/register-annotations.ts) runs before every source-count check and throws annotation_flag_like_value, naming the swallowed option's own form. A retry is offered only when dropping the text flag leaves exactly one valid source (no other alias, --add-json, --stdin, --file, --delete, or --edit with --if-absent). The CLI repair (src/cli/runtime/annotation-option-retry.ts) rebuilds it from the typed argv and withdraws it when the bindings would change, the text flag repeats, or the pair precedes the annotation command. Codex review rounds 1-4 hardened the retry paths."
expected_result: "pm comments|notes|learnings <id> --add --file <path> refuses with annotation_flag_like_value naming --file, and the suggested retry appends the file to the same item"
actual_result: Built-CLI spec replays suggested_retry_args for all three commands and each appends the file text; --stdin with an operand names the operand and offers no retry; negative control restores the old positional/--add message
affected_version: 2026.11.7
component: annotations
