comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T17:52:51.175Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented on branch fix/cli-option-contract-truthfulness. assertNoSwallowedAnnotationOption (src/cli/register-annotations.ts) runs right after the transposed-subcommand check and before every source-count check, for every text alias of comments, notes and learnings. It throws createFlagLikeAnnotationValueRefusal (src/sdk/annotations.ts), which names a swallowed --file or --stdin in its own form (\"drop --add and pass --file <path> on its own\") and, for --stdin or --file=<path> followed by an operand, names the operand that cannot be combined with it. A retry is offered only when dropping the text flag leaves exactly one source; the CLI recovery repair (src/cli/runtime/annotation-option-retry.ts, wired in repairInvocationRecovery and excluded from message-text inference) rewrites it as the typed argv minus the text flag, so tracker scope, --message, --author and --json stay, and withdraws it when the argv holds zero or two swallowing pairs. Direct SDK callers get the same source-form guidance with placeholder examples.\n\nVerification: the built-CLI spec runs the prescribed suggested_retry_args for comments, notes and learnings and each one appends the file text; it also covers --add --stdin x (named operand, no retry) and --add --stdin (retry run with piped stdin). The in-process spec covers every branch, with a negative control that disables the check (vi.doMock) and gets the old \"positional [text] or with --add\" message back. The unit spec for the repair covers rewrite, attached --add=--file, withdrawal (no pair, two pairs, after --, no command token) and pass-through. The full suite passed 12,202 of 12,203; the one failure was a host npm-path issue in an unrelated spec, and it passes with NODE_PATH set.\n"
  "2026-11-07T18:21:53.910Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 1 found two retry gaps here, both fixed in commit c6210382d. (1) P1: pm item comments --add --file pm-one pm-two parses id=pm-one with text pm-two, but dropping --add yields --file pm-one pm-two, which would read the file pm-one into item pm-two. The repair now requires the producer's intended option and operand at the rewritten position and withdraws the retry otherwise. (2) An earlier --add hello (overwritten by Commander), another text alias, or --add-json made the retry a two-source invocation. The producer now offers no retry when another alias or --add-json is present, and the repair withdraws when the text flag appears again in the argv.\n"
  "2026-11-07T18:40:45.791Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 2 found one retry gap, fixed in commit 8f4c6f6ba: an annotation text flag a namespace parent consumed (pm item --add=--stdin comments pm-one, possible when an extension adds --add to item) produced a retry that dispatches nowhere, because item does not declare --stdin. The repair now rewrites only a pair after the annotation command's own token and withdraws the retry otherwise."
  "2026-11-07T18:57:02.486Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 3 found two retry paths, fixed in commit 0ea4615fe: an option before the annotation command token (its value could look like the command) now withdraws the retry, and --delete, which takes no text, never gets a text-source retry."
